# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 288-291 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, RUN 3, 2026-09-26): THE LEVIRATE — the brother not in his world,
# the paternal brother, one widow not two and every descendant, the shoe or the marriage and no bill, the act in error or by force, the fifteen women of
# Yevamot 1:1 (288); the eldest's duty, the barren woman, the succession of the dead, the eunuch, the Omnipresent's refusal in three clauses, the doubled words,
# the high court, name is inheritance and seed, not among proselytes (289); the elders' summons and counsel, standing (290); THE RITE — the visible spittle, the
# shoe's size, the right foot and the knee, the three acts' table, the holy tongue, R. Eliezer and R. Akiva, the court of Israel, the shout (291). Every row READ
# WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(288, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN BROTHERS DWELL TOGETHER" (25:5) — EXCLUDING THE WIFE OF A BROTHER WHO WAS NOT IN HIS WORLD; HENCE: TWO BROTHERS, ONE DIED, A BROTHER WAS BORN TO THEM, THEN THE SECOND TOOK HER — ETC., THE MISHNAH. The head row of piska 288 ({SP_(288, 1, "פרט", "לאשת", "אחיו", "שלא", "היה", "בעולמו")} "excluding the wife of a brother who was not in his world"; {SP_(288, 1, "ונולד", "להם", "אח")} "and a brother was born to them"; {SP_(288, 1, "ואחר", "כך", "יבם", "השני")} "and then the second took her in levirate"): THE FIRST CONDITION OF THE LEVIRATE DAEMON — the brothers alive together; THE MISHNAH BY ABBREVIATION (Yevamot 2:1 — the English supplies the case\'s end in braces), the sitting\'s fifth; the design\'s DV25-03. Fresh.')
srow(288, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TOGETHER" — EXCLUDING HIS BROTHER FROM THE MOTHER; SINCE THE TORAH HAS BROTHERS WHERE THE MOTHER\'S BROTHER IS AS THE FATHER\'S, HERE TOO? "TOGETHER" — THE MOTHER\'S EXCLUDED. ({SP_(288, 2, "פרט", "לאחיו", "מאמו")} "excluding his brother from the mother"; {SP_(288, 2, "אח", "מן", "האם", "כאח", "מן", "האב")} "a brother from the mother as a brother from the father"): the paternal line the parameter — "together" in one inheritance. Fresh.')
srow(288, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ONE OF THEM DIES" — ONLY TWO BROTHERS? MANY — WHENCE? "ONE OF THEM"; ALL DIED? "ONE OF THEM"; WHY "ONE"? THE WIFE OF ONE IS TAKEN, NOT THE WIFE OF TWO; HENCE: THREE BROTHERS MARRIED TO THREE UNRELATED WOMEN, ONE DIED, THE SECOND MADE HER A DECLARATION AND DIED — THEY LOOSEN THE SHOE AND ARE NOT TAKEN. "AND HE HAS NO SON" — A SON\'S SON, A SON\'S DAUGHTER, A DAUGHTER\'S SON, A DAUGHTER\'S DAUGHTER WHENCE? "NO SON" — NONE AT ALL; WHY "SON"? EXCLUDING A CHILD BY THE SLAVE-GIRL OR THE GENTILE WOMAN. ({SP_(288, 3, "אשת", "אחד", "מתיבמת", "ולא", "אשת", "שנים")} "the wife of one is taken in levirate, and not the wife of two"; {SP_(288, 3, "שלשה", "אחים", "נשואים", "שלש", "נשים", "נכריות")} "three brothers married to three unrelated women"; {SP_(288, 3, "חולצות", "ולא", "מתיבמות")} "they loosen the shoe and are not taken"; {SP_(288, 3, "בן", "הבן", "ובת", "הבן", "ובן", "הבת", "ובת", "הבת")} "a son\'s son, a son\'s daughter, a daughter\'s son, a daughter\'s daughter"; {SP_(288, 3, "מן", "השפחה", "ומן", "הנכרית")} "from the slave-girl or from the gentile woman"): THE PARSER\'S [1] "ONE OF THEM" read as ONE BOND — a widow bound to two dead brothers is freed by the shoe (Yevamot 3:9 the answer sheet\'s row, the English\'s "="); "no son" means no descendant of any degree, the slave\'s and the gentile\'s children not counted — the daemon\'s second condition with its class. Fresh.')
srow(288, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE DEAD MAN\'S WIFE SHALL NOT BE OUTSIDE TO A STRANGER" — WHY NEEDED? LEST "THE WIFE OF ONE, NOT OF TWO" BE READ HERE; WHAT DOES SHE DO? SHE LOOSENS THE SHOE OR IS TAKEN. ONE WHO GIVES A BILL TO HIS LEVIRATE WIDOW DISQUALIFIES HER FOR HIMSELF AND FOR THE BROTHERS; DOES THE BILL FREE HER? THE ARGUMENT FROM THE SHOE SAYS YES — THE TEACHING SAYS "NOT OUTSIDE TO A STRANGER" EXCEPT BY THE SHOE-LOOSENING. ({SP_(288, 4, "או", "חולצת", "או", "מתיבמת")} "either she loosens the shoe or is taken"; {SP_(288, 4, "הנותן", "גט", "ליבמתו")} "he who gives a bill to his levirate widow"; {SP_(288, 4, "פסלה", "לעצמו", "ופסלה", "על", "ידי", "אחים")} "disqualified her for himself and for the brothers"; {SP_(288, 4, "אלא", "בחליצה")} "only by the shoe-loosening"): THE TWO EXITS ONLY — the marriage or the rite; the divorce bill (24:1) no release from the levirate bond though it disqualifies (270:8\'s twin); THE ENGLISH ROW 288:4 CARRIES A FIFTH SECTION (the declaration, ma\'amar — "penetration concludes the acquisition, the declaration does not") WITH NO HEBREW IN THE EXPORT\'S ROW — the third misplacement of the sitting. Fresh.')
srow(288, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"HER LEVIR SHALL COME TO HER" — IN ERROR OR WITH INTENT, BY FORCE OR WILLINGLY, EVEN HE IN ERROR AND SHE WITH INTENT OR THE REVERSE. ({SP_(288, 5, "בין", "בשוגג", "בין", "במזיד", "בין", "באנס", "בין", "ברצון")} "whether in error or with intent, whether by force or willingly"): Yevamot 6:1\'s row (the English\'s "cf.") — the act alone acquires, intention no parameter; Onkelos writes the verb plain (25:5\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(288, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND TAKE HER … AND MARRY HER" — NOT "TAKE" AND "MARRY" — EXCLUDING THE RIVAL WIFE OF ANY FORBIDDEN KIN; HENCE: FIFTEEN WOMEN FREE THEIR RIVALS AND THEIR RIVALS\' RIVALS FROM THE SHOE-LOOSENING AND THE LEVIRATE. ({SP_(288, 6, "פרט", "לצרת", "כל", "העריות")} "excluding the rival wife of any forbidden kin"; {SP_(288, 6, "חמש", "עשרה", "נשים", "פוטרות", "צרותיהן")} "fifteen women free their rivals"; {SP_(288, 6, "מן", "החליצה", "ומן", "היבום")} "from the shoe-loosening and from the levirate"): YEVAMOT 1:1 — THE TRACTATE\'S OPENING ROW IN THE SPINE (the English\'s "//"): the pronoun suffixes ("her", "her") the exclusion\'s hook; the forbidden kin\'s rival freed — the daemon\'s exception table (the design). Fresh.')
srow(289, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE FIRSTBORN SHE BEARS" (25:6) — IF HIS NAME WAS YOSE IS THE CHILD CALLED YOSE, YOHANAN YOHANAN? "SHALL STAND ON HIS BROTHER\'S NAME" — ANY NAME; WHY "THE FIRSTBORN"? THE COMMANDMENT IS ON THE ELDEST TO TAKE HER. The head row of piska 289 ({SP_(289, 1, "אם", "היה", "שמו", "יוסי", "יקרא", "שמו", "יוסי")} "if his name was Yose, is he called Yose?"; {SP_(289, 1, "שמצוה", "בגדול", "ליבם")} "the commandment is on the eldest to take her in levirate"): THE FIRSTBORN IS THE ELDEST BROTHER, not the child, and the name no literal name — Yevamot 2:8 and 4:5 the answer sheet\'s rows (the English\'s "="); Genesis 38\'s Judah read back (Er, Onan, Shelah in order). Fresh.')
srow(289, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"SHE BEARS" — EXCLUDING THE BARREN WOMAN (AYLONIT), WHO IS NOT FIT TO BEAR. ({SP_(289, 2, "פרט", "לאילונית")} "excluding the barren woman (aylonit)"; {SP_(289, 2, "שאינה", "ראויה", "לילד")} "who is not fit to bear"): the one fertility exclusion (289:7 keeps the rest). Fresh.')
srow(289, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"SHALL STAND ON HIS BROTHER\'S NAME" — AND NOT ON HIS FATHER\'S BROTHER\'S. ({SP_(289, 3, "ולא", "על", "שם", "אחי", "אביו")} "and not on his father\'s brother\'s name"): the bond one generation deep. Fresh.')
srow(289, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE DEAD" — SINCE "THE WIFE OF ONE, NOT OF TWO", WHENCE THAT IF THE FIRST DIED THE SECOND TAKES HER, THE SECOND DIED THE THIRD? "THE DEAD", "THE DEAD" — IT INCLUDES. ({SP_(289, 4, "מת", "ראשון", "ייבם", "שני")} "the first died, the second takes her"; {SP_(289, 4, "מת", "שני", "ייבם", "שלישי")} "the second died, the third takes her"; {SP_(289, 4, "המת", "המת", "רבה")} "\'the dead\', \'the dead\' — it includes"): THE SUCCESSION by the word said in both verses (25:5-6) — Judah\'s three sons the tape\'s own case (Genesis 38:8-11). Fresh.')
srow(289, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT HIS NAME BE NOT BLOTTED OUT OF ISRAEL" — EXCLUDING THE EUNUCH, WHOSE NAME IS ALREADY BLOTTED. ({SP_(289, 5, "פרט", "לסריס")} "excluding a eunuch"; {SP_(289, 5, "שכבר", "שמו", "מחוי")} "whose name is already blotted"): Yevamot 8:4 (the English\'s "cf.") — "blot out" (machah) the verb of Amalek\'s memory at 25:19 and Exodus 17:14: the same root for the childless name and the enemy\'s record. Fresh.')
srow(289, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF THE MAN DOES NOT DESIRE" (25:7) — AND NOT WHEN THE OMNIPRESENT DOES NOT DESIRE HER: THE KIN LIABLE TO DEATH BY THE COURT EXCLUDED; THOSE LIABLE TO EXCISION? "MY LEVIR REFUSES" — NOT WHEN THE OMNIPRESENT REFUSES; THOSE UNDER A PROHIBITION? "HE WILL NOT CONSENT" — NOT WHEN THE OMNIPRESENT DOES NOT CONSENT. ({SP_(289, 6, "ולא", "שלא", "חפץ", "בה", "המקום")} "and not when the Omnipresent does not desire her"; {SP_(289, 6, "מיתת", "בית", "דין")} "death by the court"; {SP_(289, 6, "כרת", "בידי", "שמים")} "excision by the hand of Heaven"; {SP_(289, 6, "שהן", "בלא", "תעשה")} "which are under a prohibition"): THE THREE SANCTION CLASSES (248:2-4\'s ladder) each excluded from the levirate by one of the verse\'s three refusal clauses — the forbidden widow exempt, the exception table\'s ground (288:6); 25:7 carries no head. Fresh.')
srow(289, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO TAKE HIS LEVIRATE WIDOW" — WHY NEEDED? SINCE "THE FIRSTBORN SHE BEARS", MIGHT I EXCLUDE THE BARREN, THE OLD AND THE MINOR, UNFIT TO BEAR? "HIS LEVIRATE WIDOW", "HIS LEVIRATE WIDOW" — IT INCLUDES. ({SP_(289, 7, "עקרה", "וזקנה", "וקטנה")} "a barren woman, an old woman and a minor"; {SP_(289, 7, "יבמתו", "יבמתו", "רבה")} "\'his levirate widow\', \'his levirate widow\' — it includes"): the doubled noun includes what 289:2 seemed to exclude — only the aylonit out, the old and the minor in; the fertility parameter narrowed to one class. Fresh.')
srow(289, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HIS LEVIRATE WIDOW GOES UP TO THE GATE" — THE COMMANDMENT IS WITH THE COURT, THE HIGHEST IN THE CITY, WITH ELDERS. ({SP_(289, 8, "מצוה", "בבית", "דין")} "the commandment is with the court"; {SP_(289, 8, "בגבוה", "שבעיר")} "at the highest in the city"; {SP_(289, 8, "בזקנים")} "with elders"): THE COURT\'S ARM in the rite — "goes up" the height; Onkelos "the gate of the court" (25:7\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(289, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"MY LEVIR REFUSES" — NOT WHEN THE OMNIPRESENT REFUSES; "TO RAISE UP FOR HIS BROTHER" — EXCLUDING THE EUNUCH, WHO IF HE WISHED COULD NOT; "A NAME" — R. JUDAH: "NAME" SAID HERE AND THERE (25:6) — AS THERE IT IS INHERITANCE, SO HERE; AS HERE IT IS SEED, SO THERE. ({SP_(289, 9, "שאם", "רצה", "להקים", "אינו", "יכול")} "who, if he wished to raise up, could not"; {SP_(289, 9, "נאמר", "כאן", "שם", "ונאמר", "להלן", "שם")} "\'name\' is said here and said there"; {SP_(289, 9, "נחלה")} "inheritance"; {SP_(289, 9, "זרע")} "seed"): THE NAME IS THE INHERITANCE AND THE SEED — a verbal analogy in both directions (264:1\'s form): THE LEVIR\'S FIRSTBORN INHERITS THE DEAD BROTHER\'S ESTATE — the daemon\'s effect on the ledger (the design\'s (b)). Fresh.')
srow(289, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN ISRAEL" — AND NOT AMONG PROSELYTES; HENCE: TWO PROSELYTE BROTHERS CONCEIVED OUTSIDE HOLINESS AND BORN IN HOLINESS ARE EXEMPT FROM THE SHOE-LOOSENING AND THE LEVIRATE. ({SP_(289, 10, "ולא", "בגרים")} "and not among proselytes"; {SP_(289, 10, "שהיתה", "הורתם", "שלא", "בקדשה", "ולידתם", "בקדשה")} "whose conception was not in holiness and whose birth was in holiness"; {SP_(289, 10, "פטורים", "מן", "החליצה", "ומן", "היבום")} "exempt from the shoe-loosening and from the levirate"): the brotherhood dated from the conversion — a status by the mother\'s state at conception (Yevamot 11:2\'s case; the English\'s "cf. 8:2" the cite to check at the compile). Fresh.')
srow(289, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE WILL NOT CONSENT TO TAKE ME" — AND NOT WHEN THE OMNIPRESENT DOES NOT CONSENT TO HER. ({SP_(289, 11, "ולא", "שלא", "אבה", "בה", "המקום")} "and not when the Omnipresent did not consent to her"): the third refusal clause for itself (289:6) — the piska\'s last row. Fresh.')
srow(290, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE ELDERS OF HIS CITY CALL HIM" (25:8) — THE COMMANDMENT IS WITH THE ELDERS OF HIS CITY. The head row of piska 290 ({SP_(290, 1, "מצוה", "בזקני", "עירו")} "the commandment is with the elders of his city"): the summons the court\'s — his city\'s, not hers. Fresh.')
srow(290, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SPEAK TO HIM" — OF WHAT IS FITTING FOR HIM: IF HE IS A BOY AND SHE OLD, OR HE OLD AND SHE A GIRL, THEY SAY "GO TO ONE LIKE YOURSELF; WHY BRING STRIFE INTO YOUR HOUSE?" ({SP_(290, 2, "בהוגנת", "לו")} "about what is fitting for him"; {SP_(290, 2, "הוא", "ילד", "והיא", "זקנה")} "he a boy and she old"; {SP_(290, 2, "כלך", "אצל", "כמותך")} "go to one like yourself"; {SP_(290, 2, "להכניס", "קטטה", "לביתך")} "to bring strife into your house"): THE ELDERS\' COUNSEL against an unfit match — Yevamot 12:6\'s row (the English\'s "//"); the court may advise the refusal. Fresh.')
srow(290, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE STANDS AND SAYS" — HE SAYS HIS WORDS ONLY STANDING. ({SP_(290, 3, "אלא", "בעמידה")} "only standing"): the posture of the declaration (the Tosefta\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(290, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"I DO NOT DESIRE TO TAKE HER" — AND NOT WHEN THE OMNIPRESENT DOES NOT DESIRE HER. ({SP_(290, 4, "ולא", "שלא", "חפץ", "בה", "המקום")} "and not when the Omnipresent does not desire her"): the refusal formula\'s fourth seat (289:6, 289:9, 289:11) — his words, not Heaven\'s bar. Fresh.')
srow(291, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HIS LEVIRATE WIDOW COMES NEAR HIM BEFORE THE ELDERS\' EYES AND SPITS BEFORE HIM" (25:9) — SPITTLE VISIBLE TO THE ELDERS; "BEFORE THE EYES" — SHE IS TOGETHER WITH HIM BEFORE THEM. The head row of piska 291 ({SP_(291, 1, "רק", "הנראה", "לעיני", "הזקנים")} "spittle visible to the elders\' eyes"; {SP_(291, 1, "שמתיחדת", "עמו")} "that she is together with him"): the rite\'s witnesses — the court sees the spittle and the pair. Fresh.')
srow(291, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND DRAWS OFF HIS SHOE" — ONLY HIS OWN? OTHERS\' WHENCE? "THE HOUSE OF THE LOOSED SHOE" (25:10) — ANY; WHY "HIS SHOE"? EXCLUDING ONE TOO BIG TO WALK IN, TOO SMALL TO COVER MOST OF THE FOOT, OR A SANDAL WITHOUT A HEEL — HER LOOSENING INVALID. ({SP_(291, 2, "של", "אחרים", "מנין")} "of others — whence?"; {SP_(291, 2, "פרט", "לגדול", "שאין", "יכול", "להלך", "בו")} "excluding one too big to walk in"; {SP_(291, 2, "וסולייס", "שאין", "לו", "עקב")} "and a sandal without a heel"; {SP_(291, 2, "שחליצתה", "פסולה")} "her loosening is invalid"): THE SHOE\'S PARAMETERS — Yevamot 12:1-2 (the English\'s "cf.") — the shoe an EFFECT with a fitness test (the design\'s DV25-03). Fresh.')
srow(291, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM HIS FOOT" — "FOOT" SAID HERE AND THERE (LEVITICUS 14:14): AS THERE THE RIGHT, SO HERE THE RIGHT; "FROM HIS FOOT" — FROM THE KNEE DOWN VALID, FROM THE KNEE UP INVALID. ({SP_(291, 3, "ימנית")} "the right"; {SP_(291, 3, "מן", "הארכבה", "ולמטה", "חליצתה", "כשרה")} "from the knee down her loosening is valid"; {SP_(291, 3, "מן", "הארכבה", "ולמעלה", "חליצתה", "פסולה")} "from the knee up her loosening is invalid"): THE LEPER\'S RIGHT FOOT (Leviticus 14:14 — 24:8\'s daemon) lends the rite its side by a verbal analogy; Yevamot 12:1\'s knee (the English\'s "//"). Fresh.')
srow(291, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SPITS BEFORE HIM" — LITERALLY IN HIS FACE? "BEFORE THE ELDERS\' EYES" — VISIBLE TO THEM; HENCE: LOOSENED AND SPAT AND DID NOT RECITE — VALID; RECITED AND SPAT AND DID NOT LOOSEN — INVALID; LOOSENED AND RECITED AND DID NOT SPIT — R. ELIEZER INVALID, R. AKIVA VALID. ({SP_(291, 4, "יכול", "בפניו", "ממש")} "might it be literally in his face?"; {SP_(291, 4, "חלצה", "ורקקה", "ולא", "קראתה")} "she loosened and spat and did not recite"; {SP_(291, 4, "קראתה", "ורקקה", "ולא", "חלצה")} "she recited and spat and did not loosen"; {SP_(291, 4, "חלצה", "וקראתה", "ולא", "רקקה")} "she loosened and recited and did not spit"): Yevamot 12:3 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — THE RITE\'S THREE ACTS AND THEIR NECESSITY: the shoe essential, the recital not, the spittle disputed — the compile\'s effects table (the shoe and the spittle EFFECTS, the design). Fresh.')
srow(291, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ANSWERS AND SAYS" — "ANSWERING" SAID HERE AND THERE (27:15): AS THERE IN THE HOLY TONGUE, SO HERE IN THE HOLY TONGUE. ({SP_(291, 5, "נאמרה", "כאן", "עניה", "ונאמרה", "להלן", "עניה")} "\'answering\' is said here and said there"; {SP_(291, 5, "בלשון", "הקדש")} "in the holy tongue"): THE RECITAL IN HEBREW by analogy to the Levites\' answer of 27:15 — A VERSE AHEAD (the pointer for 27:15 owed with 24:16\'s and 25:19\'s); Sotah 7:2\'s list of recitals (the English\'s "cf."). Fresh.')
srow(291, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"THUS SHALL BE DONE TO THE MAN WHO WILL NOT BUILD HIS BROTHER\'S HOUSE" — R. ELIEZER: WHO DID NOT BUILD AND WILL NOT BUILD. ({SP_(291, 6, "אשר", "לא", "בנה", "ואשר", "לא", "עתיד", "לבנות")} "who did not build and who will not build"): after the shoe no levirate ever — the refusal final (the status the rite sets). Fresh.')
srow(291, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER: "THUS SHALL BE DONE" — A THING WHOSE ACT IS ESSENTIAL; R. AKIVA: FROM THERE A PROOF? "THUS SHALL BE DONE TO THE MAN" — WHAT IS DONE TO THE MAN; R. SHIMON: THE LOOSENING ESSENTIAL AND THE SPITTING ESSENTIAL; "HIS NAME SHALL BE CALLED IN ISRAEL" (25:10) — R. ISHMAEL: THE LOOSENING FOR THE LYING, THE SPITTING FOR THE SEED. ({SP_(291, 7, "בדבר", "שמעשה", "מעכב")} "a thing whose act is essential"; {SP_(291, 7, "משם", "ראיה")} "from there a proof?"; {SP_(291, 7, "חליצה", "מעכבת", "ורקיקה", "מעכבת")} "the loosening is essential and the spitting is essential"; {SP_(291, 7, "חליצה", "בשכיבה", "ורקיקה", "כדי", "שכבת", "זרע")} "the loosening for the lying, the spitting for the seed"): 291:4\'s dispute argued from the verse\'s "thus"; R. Ishmael\'s reading of the two acts as signs of the refused marriage; 25:10 carries no head. Fresh.')
srow(291, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"HIS NAME SHALL BE CALLED IN ISRAEL" — "IN ISRAEL" SAID HERE AND THERE (25:7): AS THERE IT EXCLUDES A COURT OF PROSELYTES, SO HERE. ({SP_(291, 8, "פרט", "לבית", "דין", "של", "גרים")} "excluding a court of proselytes"): the analogy inside the chapter — 289:10\'s "not among proselytes" carried to the judges: the court\'s composition a parameter. Fresh.')
srow(291, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE HOUSE OF THE LOOSED SHOE" — THE COMMANDMENT IS ON THE JUDGES, NOT ON THE DISCIPLES; R. JUDAH: ON ALL WHO STAND THERE TO SAY "LOOSED OF THE SHOE, LOOSED OF THE SHOE"; R. JUDAH: ONCE WE SAT BEFORE R. TARFON AND HE SAID "ANSWER, ALL OF YOU: LOOSED OF THE SHOE!" ({SP_(291, 9, "מצוה", "בדינים", "ולא", "מצוה", "בתלמידים")} "the commandment is on the judges and not on the disciples"; {SP_(291, 9, "חלוץ", "הנעל", "חלוץ", "הנעל")} "loosed of the shoe, loosed of the shoe"; {SP_(291, 9, "היינו", "יושבים", "לפני", "רבי", "טרפון")} "we were sitting before R. Tarfon"): THE SHOUT the rite\'s close — the name given aloud (Yevamot 12:6\'s row; the English\'s "M. Yev. 12:10" a cite past the tractate\'s twelfth chapter\'s count — to check at the compile); the piska\'s and the levirate\'s last row. Fresh.')
